In computing adjusted income the following amounts shall be added to unadjusted income:
(1) interest from bonds, notes, and other evidences of indebtedness issued by any state of the United States, including any agency and instrumentality of a state of the United States;
(2) the amount of any deduction taken on a corporation's federal return for taxes paid by a corporation:
(2)(a) to Utah for taxes imposed by this chapter; and
(2)(b) to another state of the United States, a foreign country, a United States possession, or the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico for taxes imposed for the privilege of doing business, or exercising its corporate franchise, including income, franchise, corporate stock and business and occupation taxes;
(3) the safe harbor lease adjustment required under Subsections 59-7-111(1)(a) and (2)(a);
(4) capital losses that have been deducted on a Utah corporate return in previous years;
(5) any deduction on the federal return that has been previously deducted on the Utah return;
(6) charitable contributions, to the extent deducted on the federal return when determining federal taxable income;
(7) the amount of gain or loss determined under Section 59-7-114 relating to a target corporation under Section 338, Internal Revenue Code, unless such gain or loss has already been included in the unadjusted income of the target corporation;
(8) the amount of gain or loss determined under Section 59-7-115 relating to corporations treated for federal purposes as having disposed of its assets under Section 336(e), Internal Revenue Code, unless such gain or loss has already been included in the unadjusted income of the target corporation;
(9) adjustments to gains, losses, depreciation expense, amortization expense, and similar items due to a difference between basis for federal purposes and basis as computed under Section 59-7-107;
(10) the amount withdrawn under Title 53H, Chapter 10, Utah Education Savings, from the account of a corporation that is an account owner as defined in Section 53H-10-101, for the taxable year for which the amount is withdrawn, if that amount withdrawn from the account of the corporation that is the account owner:
(10)(a) is not expended for:
(10)(a)(i) higher education costs as defined in Section 53H-10-201; or
(10)(a)(ii) a payment or distribution that qualifies as an exception to the additional tax for distributions not used for educational expenses provided in Sections 529(c) and 530(d), Internal Revenue Code; and
(10)(b) is subtracted by the corporation:
(10)(b)(i) that is the account owner; and
(10)(b)(ii) in accordance with Subsection 59-7-106(1)(r);
(11) the amount of the deduction for dividends paid, as defined in Section 561, Internal Revenue Code, that is allowed under Section 857(b)(2)(B), Internal Revenue Code, in computing the taxable income of a captive real estate investment trust, if that captive real estate investment trust is subject to federal income taxation; and
(12) any deduction on a return filed under this chapter for a royalty or other expense that a corporation pays to an entity related by common ownership for the use of an intangible asset where the intangible asset is owned by the entity related by common ownership unless the corporation can demonstrate to the satisfaction of the commission or a court on judicial review in accordance with Section 59-1-602 or Title 63G, Chapter 4, Part 4, Judicial Review, that:
(12)(a) for the same taxable year, the entity related by common ownership is subject to income taxes on the royalty or other expense:
(12)(a)(i) under this chapter;
(12)(a)(ii) under the laws of another state; or
(12)(a)(iii) by a foreign government that has in force an income tax treaty with the United States; or
(12)(b) if Subsection (12)(a) does not apply, the corporation paying the royalty or other expenses never owned the intangible asset.

(1) In computing adjusted income, the following amounts shall be subtracted from unadjusted income:
(1)(a) the foreign dividend gross-up included in gross income for federal income tax purposes under Section 78, Internal Revenue Code;
(1)(b) subject to Subsection (2), the net capital loss, as defined for federal purposes, if the taxpayer elects to deduct the net capital loss on the return filed under this chapter for the taxable year for which the net capital loss is incurred;
(1)(c) the decrease in salary expense deduction for federal income tax purposes due to claiming the federal work opportunity credit under Section 51, Internal Revenue Code;
(1)(d) the decrease in qualified research and basic research expense deduction for federal income tax purposes due to claiming the federal credit for increasing research activities under Section 41, Internal Revenue Code;
(1)(e) the decrease in qualified clinical testing expense deduction for federal income tax purposes due to claiming the federal credit for clinical testing expenses for certain drugs for rare diseases or conditions under Section 45C, Internal Revenue Code;
(1)(f) any decrease in any expense deduction for federal income tax purposes due to claiming any other federal credit;
(1)(g) the safe harbor lease adjustment required under Subsections 59-7-111(1)(b) and (2)(b);
(1)(h) any income on the federal corporation income tax return that has been previously taxed by Utah;
(1)(i) an amount included in federal taxable income that is due to a refund of a tax, including a franchise tax, an income tax, a corporate stock and business tax, or an occupation tax:
(1)(i)(i) if that tax is imposed for the privilege of:
(1)(i)(i)(A) doing business; or
(1)(i)(i)(B) exercising a corporate franchise;
(1)(i)(ii) if that tax is paid by the corporation to:
(1)(i)(ii)(A) Utah;
(1)(i)(ii)(B) another state of the United States;
(1)(i)(ii)(C) a foreign country;
(1)(i)(ii)(D) a United States possession; or
(1)(i)(ii)(E) the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico; and
(1)(i)(iii) to the extent that tax was added to unadjusted income under Section 59-7-105;
(1)(j) a charitable contribution, to the extent the charitable contribution is allowed as a subtraction under Section 59-7-109;
(1)(k) subject to Subsection (3), 50% of a dividend considered to be received or received from a subsidiary that:
(1)(k)(i) is a member of the unitary group;
(1)(k)(ii) is organized or incorporated outside of the United States; and
(1)(k)(iii) is not included in a combined report under Section 59-7-402 or 59-7-403;
(1)(l) subject to Subsection (4) and Section 59-7-401, 50% of the adjusted income of a foreign operating company;
(1)(m) the amount of gain or loss that is included in unadjusted income but not recognized for federal purposes on stock sold or exchanged by a member of a selling consolidated group as defined in Section 338, Internal Revenue Code, if an election has been made in accordance with Section 338(h)(10), Internal Revenue Code;
(1)(n) the amount of gain or loss that is included in unadjusted income but not recognized for federal purposes on stock sold, exchanged, or distributed by a corporation in accordance with Section 336(e), Internal Revenue Code, if an election under Section 336(e), Internal Revenue Code, has been made for federal purposes;
(1)(o) subject to Subsection (5), an adjustment to the following due to a difference between basis for federal purposes and basis as computed under Section 59-7-107:
(1)(o)(i) an amortization expense;
(1)(o)(ii) a depreciation expense;
(1)(o)(iii) a gain;
(1)(o)(iv) a loss; or
(1)(o)(v) an item similar to Subsections (1)(o)(i) through (iv);
(1)(p) an interest expense that is not deducted on a federal corporation income tax return under Section 265(b) or 291(e), Internal Revenue Code;
(1)(q) 100% of dividends received from a subsidiary that is an insurance company if that subsidiary that is an insurance company is:
(1)(q)(i) exempt from this chapter under Subsection 59-7-102(1)(c); and
(1)(q)(ii) under common ownership;
(1)(r) subject to Subsection 59-7-105(10), for a corporation that is an account owner as defined in Section 53H-10-101, the amount of a qualified investment as defined in Section 53H-10-201:
(1)(r)(i) that the corporation or a person other than the corporation makes into an account owned by the corporation during the taxable year;
(1)(r)(ii) to the extent that neither the corporation nor the person other than the corporation described in Subsection (1)(r)(i) deducts the qualified investment on a federal income tax return; and
(1)(r)(iii) to the extent the qualified investment does not exceed the maximum amount of the qualified investment that may be subtracted from unadjusted income for a taxable year in accordance with Subsection 53H-10-205(1);
(1)(s) for purposes of income included in a combined report under Part 4, Combined Reporting, the entire amount of the dividends a member of a unitary group receives or is considered to receive from a captive real estate investment trust;
(1)(t) the increase in income for federal income tax purposes due to claiming a:
(1)(t)(i) qualified tax credit bond credit under Section 54A, Internal Revenue Code; or
(1)(t)(ii) qualified zone academy bond under Section 1397E, Internal Revenue Code;
(1)(u) for a taxable year beginning on or after January 1, 2019, but beginning on or before December 31, 2019, only:
(1)(u)(i) the amount of any FDIC premium paid or incurred by the taxpayer that is disallowed as a deduction for federal income tax purposes under Section 162(r), Internal Revenue Code, on the taxpayer's 2018 federal income tax return; plus
(1)(u)(ii) the amount of any FDIC premium paid or incurred by the taxpayer that is disallowed as a deduction for federal income tax purposes under Section 162(r), Internal Revenue Code, for the taxable year; and
(1)(v) for a taxable year beginning on or after January 1, 2020, the amount of any FDIC premium paid or incurred by the taxpayer that is disallowed as a deduction for federal income tax purposes under Section 162(r), Internal Revenue Code, for the taxable year.
(2) For purposes of Subsection (1)(b):
(2)(a) the subtraction shall be made by claiming the subtraction on a return filed:
(2)(a)(i) under this chapter for the taxable year for which the net capital loss is incurred; and
(2)(a)(ii) by the due date of the return, including extensions; and
(2)(b) a net capital loss for a taxable year shall be:
(2)(b)(i) subtracted for the taxable year for which the net capital loss is incurred; or
(2)(b)(ii) carried forward as provided in Sections 1212(a)(1)(B) and (C), Internal Revenue Code.
(3)
(3)(a) For purposes of calculating the subtraction provided for in Subsection (1)(k), a taxpayer shall first subtract from a dividend considered to be received or received an expense directly attributable to that dividend.
(3)(b) For purposes of Subsection (3)(a), the amount of an interest expense that is considered to be directly attributable to a dividend is calculated by multiplying the interest expense by a fraction:
(3)(b)(i) the numerator of which is the taxpayer's average investment in the dividend paying subsidiaries; and
(3)(b)(ii) the denominator of which is the taxpayer's average total investment in assets.
(3)(c)
(3)(c)(i) For purposes of calculating the subtraction allowed by Subsection (1)(k), in determining income apportionable to this state, a portion of the factors of a foreign subsidiary that has dividends that are partially subtracted under Subsection (1)(k) shall be included in the combined report factors as provided in this Subsection (3)(c).
(3)(c)(ii) For purposes of Subsection (3)(c)(i), the portion of the factors of a foreign subsidiary that has dividends that are partially subtracted under Subsection (1)(k) that shall be included in the combined report factors is calculated by multiplying each factor of the foreign subsidiary by a fraction:
(3)(c)(ii)(A) not to exceed 100%; and
(3)(c)(ii)(B)
(3)(c)(ii)(B)(I) the numerator of which is the amount of the dividend paid by the foreign subsidiary that is included in adjusted income; and
(3)(c)(ii)(B)(II) the denominator of which is the current year earnings and profits of the foreign subsidiary as determined under the Internal Revenue Code.
(3)(d) A dividend described in Subsection (1)(k) includes amounts included in federal taxable income under Section 965(a), Internal Revenue Code and amounts included in federal taxable income under Section 951A, Internal Revenue Code.
(4)
(4)(a) For purposes of Subsection (1)(l), a taxpayer may not make a subtraction under Subsection (1)(l):
(4)(a)(i) if the taxpayer elects to file a worldwide combined report as provided in Section 59-7-403; or
(4)(a)(ii) for the following:
(4)(a)(ii)(A) income generated from intangible property; or
(4)(a)(ii)(B) a capital gain, dividend, interest, rent, royalty, or other similar item that is generated from an asset held for investment and not from a regular business trading activity.
(4)(b) In calculating the subtraction provided for in Subsection (1)(l), a foreign operating company:
(4)(b)(i) may not subtract an amount provided for in Subsection (1)(k) or (l); and
(4)(b)(ii) prior to determining the subtraction under Subsection (1)(l), shall eliminate a transaction that occurs between members of a unitary group.
(4)(c) For purposes of the subtraction provided for in Subsection (1)(l), in determining income apportionable to this state, the factors for a foreign operating company shall be included in the combined report factors in the same percentages as the foreign operating company's adjusted income is included in the combined adjusted income.
(4)(d) In accordance with Title 63G, Chapter 3, Utah Administrative Rulemaking Act, the commission may by rule define what constitutes:
(4)(d)(i) income generated from intangible property; or
(4)(d)(ii) a capital gain, dividend, interest, rent, royalty, or other similar item that is generated from an asset held for investment and not from a regular business trading activity.
(5)
(5)(a) For purposes of the subtraction provided for in Subsection (1)(o), the amount of a reduction in basis shall be allowed as an expense for the taxable year in which a federal tax credit is claimed if:
(5)(a)(i) there is a reduction in federal basis for a federal tax credit; and
(5)(a)(ii) there is no corresponding tax credit allowed in this state.
(5)(b) In accordance with Title 63G, Chapter 3, Utah Administrative Rulemaking Act, the commission may by rule define what constitutes an item similar to Subsections (1)(o)(i) through (iv).

(1) As used in this section:
(1)(a)
(1)(a)(i) "Finance lease" means a lease transaction that is the functional equivalent of an extension of credit and that transfers substantially all of the benefits and risks incident to the ownership of property.
(1)(a)(ii) "Finance lease" includes a direct financing lease or leverage lease that meets the criteria of Financial Accounting Standards Board Statement No. 13, Accounting for Leases, or any other lease that is accounted for as a financing lease by a lessor under generally accepted accounting principles.
(1)(b) "Financial institution" means:
(1)(b)(i) a corporation or other business entity registered under state law as a bank holding company, under the Federal Bank Holding Act of 1956, as amended, or registered as a savings and loan holding company under the Federal National Housing Act, as amended;
(1)(b)(ii) a national bank organized and existing as a national bank association in accordance with the National Bank Act, 12 U.S.C. Secs. 21 et seq.;
(1)(b)(iii) a savings association or federal savings bank as defined in 12 U.S.C. Secs. 1813(b)(1) and (2);
(1)(b)(iv) a bank, industrial loan corporation, or thrift institution incorporated or organized under the laws of any state;
(1)(b)(v) a corporation organized under the provisions of 12 U.S.C. Secs. 611 through 631;
(1)(b)(vi) an agency or a branch of a foreign bank as defined in 12 U.S.C. Sec. 3101;
(1)(b)(vii) a production credit association organized under the Federal Farm Credit Act of 1933, if all of the production credit association's stock held by the Federal Production Credit Corporation has been retired;
(1)(b)(viii) a corporation, other than an insurance company taxable under Chapter 9, Taxation of Admitted Insurers, for which voting stock is more than 50% owned, directly or indirectly, by any person described in Subsections (1)(b)(i) through (1)(b)(vii);
(1)(b)(ix) a corporation or other business entity that derives from finance leases more than 50% of the corporation's or the business entity's total gross income for financial accounting purposes:
(1)(b)(ix)(A) using the average of the gross income in the current tax year and immediately preceding two tax years; and
